## 6. A release tag deploys too, and the previous release stays for rollback
   concept: gitlab-ci-local --needs deploy runs deploy and what it depends on (build, which has no needs:, so every earlier stage); rolling back is pointing current at the previous release
   deploy > smoke ok
   deploy > deployed v1.4.0 to .deploy/current
    PASS  lint
    PASS  typecheck
    PASS  unit
    PASS  a11y
    PASS  audit
    PASS  build
    PASS  deploy
   pipeline finished in 52 s
   current -> releases/v1.4.0, release.json {"release":"v1.4.0","commit":"297ddab1b3b52766b565af7d1bf1ec344a175371","source":"push"}; previous releases/scheduled-297ddab1-1002 still on disk: true

## 7. The same pipeline on GitHub Actions
   concept: github-actions/ci.yml (not under .github/, so it does not run here) has the same jobs and commands; stages become needs, rules become if, resource_group becomes concurrency
   job        gitlab stage  github needs  commands
   lint       lint                        npm run lint
   typecheck  typecheck     lint          npm run typecheck
   unit       test          typecheck     npx vitest run
   a11y       test          typecheck     npm run a11y
   audit      audit         unit, a11y    npm run audit
   build      build         audit         npm run build
   deploy     deploy        build         cp -r dist, ln -sfn
   deploy when, gitlab: [{"if":"$CI_PIPELINE_SOURCE == \"schedule\""},{"if":"$CI_COMMIT_TAG =~ /^v\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+$/"}]
   deploy when, github: github.event_name == 'schedule' || startsWith(github.ref, 'refs/tags/v')

